{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s","id":606808,"title":"aggravated damage source in B&S","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-29T10:36:18-07:00","id":606808,"title":"aggravated damage source in B&S","content":"Hi all, I have a question about aggravated damage. How can a kindred make aggravated damage without using fire or silver but just with his own discipline? <br /> In the first edition the claw made with protean could...but in blod&amp;smoke the claw of protean 2 deal just lethal (banshing against kindred) damage and with protean 4 lethal also against kindred. <br /> In a fight against a werewolf in warform is impossible to win cause he automatically heal ALL lethal damage. I read in the core that some kindred power deal aggravated to the werewolf but I didn' t find that power. And how can werewolf deal aggravated to the kindred ? (With what gift?) <br /> Thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T10:48:31-07:00","id":606837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s#post606808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a fight against a werewolf in warform is impossible to win cause he automatically heal ALL lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very much not impossible. It's just a matter of doing enough lethal damage to roll them over to aggravated. Without any special abilities vampires can do this with a good-sized combat dicepool, willpower, physical intensity, the bonus dice from frenzy, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I read in the core that some kindred power deal aggravated to the werewolf but I didn' t find that power. And how can werewolf deal aggravated to the kindred ? (With what gift?)<br /> Thank you </div> </div> </div>The blood sorceries Feeding the Crone and Blandishment of Sin both allow a vampire to cause aggravated damage. The latter allows any vampire to do it. The only gift that might allow a werewolf to inflict aggravated to a vampire is Tongue of Flame, which allows Influence over Fire, and possibly Shadow Masquerade, if used on a spirit of fire or sunlight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:05:35-07:00","id":606843,"title":"","content":"There's also a merit that upgrades the protean 4 claws to +0 aggravated when the vampire frenzies called Claws of the Unholy. That sounds like what you were looking for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:09:40-07:00","id":606848,"title":"","content":"combine that with a Coil To allow you to frenzy at will and you are golden. (and a scary scary monster if my memories of actual play serve)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:13:36-07:00","id":606851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606837#post606837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's very much not impossible. It's just a matter of doing enough lethal damage to roll them over to aggravated. Without any special abilities vampires can do this with a good-sized combat dicepool, willpower, physical intensity, the bonus dice from frenzy, and so on.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but a fight werewolf could easly have 15 health dot...it's hard in a turn make more than 15 damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway cause in my crhonicles the players are going in werewolf territory I would like to know better how to deal a possible fight between vampire and werewolf. Is right to say that (same stats between vampire and werewolf just to make an ipotetical and theoretical example) a vampire could be in a little advantage in a fight vs a werewolf due to theese factors:<br /> -Active Celerity that bypassing initiative let the kindred attack first<br /> -Active Vigor that add dot vigor to the damage of the attack<br /> -maybe a 2 vitae spent in strenght to rise of 4 dice the roll for the attack<br /> <br /> And with resilence eventual damage infert by the gauru would be decreased of the resilence value?<br /> <br /> And last question: Social Disciplines like Dominate or majesty could act during a fight against a Gauru or they automatically fail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:19:24-07:00","id":606857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606851#post606851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but a fight werewolf could easly have 15 health dot...it's hard in a turn make more than 15 damage <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It can just as easily be 11. But yes, it's hard to kill a werewolf in warform unless you're really good in combat. That's sort of the point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And last question: Social Disciplines like Dominate or majesty could act during a fight against a Gauru or they automatically fail? </div> </div> </div>Against a werewolf in gauru you can use all the social disciplines you want. It's Kuruth where you'll have more of a problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:25:49-07:00","id":606868,"title":"","content":"Of course, there's almost never just <i>one</i> werewolf...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:33:01-07:00","id":606873,"title":"","content":"Sort of makes you appreciate Majesty more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:36:31-07:00","id":606877,"title":"","content":"On the whole Werewolves are better combatants than Vampires in Gauru forum. The key phrase here is &quot;in Gauru form&quot;, in all other forms Werewolves are squishy, and vulnerable to normal amounts of damage (as opposed to Gauru, which is vulnerable only to absurd amounts of damage). So it behooves a Vampire to avoid direct combat in favor of ambush tactics and coercion.<br /> <br /> However, if a vampire does have to fight a Werewolf head to head, the following approaches work best:<ul><li><b>Bring Friends</b>: Gauru form is absurdly durable, a single vampire is not likely to be able to put the damage forward to pierce its regeneration. Not unless they are some twinked out combat beast. So numbers are your friend. Three people with fully automatic rifles turns the tables quite nicely, though the more the merrier in this endeavor.</li> <li><b>Bring Banes: </b>Silver hurts Werewolves, sometimes it can be enough to deter a fight outright. Remember, every aggravated damage dealt to a wolf decreases the difficulty of rolling over with lethal, so just two or three swipes with a silver knife could be enough to turn the tide (though close quarters combat is highly inadvisable).</li> <li><b>Be a Cheat: </b>Vampires are well equipped to shut down conflicts through mental tricks, Majesty can remove the enemy's incentive to fight, while Obfuscate can remove their ability to attack you (being an invisible sneak). Two dots of Nightmare shuts down just about any combatant, sending the big bad wolf running with its tail between its legs.</li> <li><b>Be a Bad Enough Dude: </b>A suitably combat spec'd Vampire can do toe to toe with a Werewolf, even a very potent one. But this sort of character will probably be rare among PCs, requiring many dots worth of disciplines and devotions to pull off.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:36:49-07:00","id":606878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606868#post606868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, there's almost never just <i>one</i> werewolf...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I know but also the coteries of vampires is composed from more then one vampire. Mine was an example to understand the mechanics of a fight between these two race and in order to balance an eventual encounter<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:40:49-07:00","id":606888,"title":"","content":"If an entire pack goes into rage, anyone who fights them is likely to die, unless they're overwhelmingly powerful to begin with.<br /> <br /> Of course you can always run away, since you're not getting experience by the corpse.<br /> <br /> But werewolves in general aren't likely to attack vampires on sight, or without good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:44:30-07:00","id":606891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606877#post606877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole Werewolves are better combatants than Vampires in Gauru forum. The key phrase here is &quot;in Gauru form&quot;, in all other forms Werewolves are squishy, and vulnerable to normal amounts of damage (as opposed to Gauru, which is vulnerable only to absurd amounts of damage). So it behooves a Vampire to avoid direct combat in favor of ambush tactics and coercion.[*]<b>Be a Bad Enough Dude: </b>A suitably combat spec'd Vampire can do toe to toe with a Werewolf, even a very potent one. But this sort of character will probably be rare among PCs, requiring many dots worth of disciplines and devotions to pull off.[/LIST]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Agree with all your point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But could you be more specific about this combat spec'd vampire to stand against a Gauru? Just to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I think you menas: Vigor celerity and resilence obviously and probably protean and what else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T11:58:05-07:00","id":606898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606891#post606891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agree with all your point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But could you be more specific about this combat spec'd vampire to stand against a Gauru? Just to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I think you menas: Vigor celerity and resilence obviously and probably protean and what else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly, though all of those will certainly help. nWoD is pretty good about not having &quot;optimal&quot; builds.<br /> <br /> For instance, a PC vampire did quite well with Celerity 5, Resilience 2, and five dots of the Light Weapons fighting style (Using the feint and thrust maneuvers to deal damage, while relying on Celerity to negate the defense loss). NPCs have included giant bat monster (Vigor + Protean + Frenzy, swoop down, grapple, drag to the clouds), Invisible Sniper Bro (Celerity + Praestantia + Obfuscate 3 &amp; a big old rifle), and The Invincible 1st Ed Foe (Resilience &amp; Vigor 5 with that 1st ed devotion that turns Vigor dots into more Resilience [don't do this]).<br /> <br /> One can get terrific mileage out of Protean 5, not many characters are equipped to deal with murder fog. Similarly don't underestimate the power of Animalism, four dots in and you can (storyteller permitting) control those raging wolves outright. Dominate 5 removes much of the risk of direct encounter (by removing the direct portion of it), as can Majesty.<br /> <br /> Oh, I forgot to mention mortal weaponry. Never underestimate mortal weaponry. Invisible sniper bro (see above) performed absolute sorcery with some obfuscated explosives (Semtex and claymores). Assuming your game is set in the US, vampires have lots of tools for getting their hands on big, illegal firearms. Barring those a couple molotov cocktails hurled on wolfie will certainly rack up some damage (yes, it's fire, but beggers can't be choosers when being run down by an eight foot wolfman)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 07-29-2015, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T12:22:46-07:00","id":606934,"title":"","content":"Thank you. You help me a lot <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T12:56:17-07:00","id":606962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s#post606808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all, I have a question about aggravated damage. How can a kindred make aggravated damage without using fire or silver but just with his own discipline?<br /> In the first edition the claw made with protean could...but in blod&amp;smoke the claw of protean 2 deal just lethal (banshing against kindred) damage and with protean 4 lethal also against kindred.<br /> In a fight against a werewolf in warform is impossible to win cause he automatically heal ALL lethal damage. I read in the core that some kindred power deal aggravated to the werewolf but I didn' t find that power. And how can werewolf deal aggravated to the kindred ? (With what gift?)<br /> Thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh... oh my! This... this is new! A vamp versus wolf thread... in the vampire forum! That NEVER happens! <br /> <br /> *Cough* <br /> <br /> Ahem, more seriously, the sorceries mentioned above and the Claws of the Unholy are your best bet if we're looking at a white room one-on-one slug fest. In practice? There's a million other tactics to try. A werewolf in the midst of Wasu-Im is a deadly, neigh unstoppable force. So, use Dominate, Majesty, whatever before hand. Keep the interaction calm. Use Obfuscate - its easier and smarter to run away from battle than engage in it. <br /> <br /> Werewolves specialize in shapeshifting, pack tactics, and the hunt. Vampires, on the other hand, specialize in underlings and controls (both physical and mental). Vampire is primarily a political-social game. So, play to the vampire's strengths, not the werewolf's. <br /> <br /> The problem is that we're not really looking at all werewolves being Blood Talon Rahu here. We're looking at some with Element (Fire) gifts, warding, ritualists... there's so many builds that, in real game, its impossible to really figure it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T13:33:57-07:00","id":607012,"title":"","content":"Just want to add that, tough Werewolf's Gauru form is impressive, a Vampire's Frenzy can also be deadly with the right tools and the right Coil of the Dragon.<br /> <br /> But all in all, MCN is right. Play to vampire strengths. Control the terrain, play social, and only attack if necessary and from advantage.<br /> <br /> And if the coterie are going into the Uratha territory, don't realy expect them to win, just to survive. The weres aren't dumb and its their home. They will have much more than just Gauru forms on their side. And will probably be the ones with Sniper Guy on their side and prepared..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:05:20-07:00","id":607075,"title":"","content":"My general rule with vampire is: if you are fighting something that isn't a mortal or a diablerie victim, something has gone horribly wrong.<br /> <br /> Werewolves barging in on your turf? Forge evidence to get them arrested. Suddenly their hideout is scheduled for demolition. The police start harassing them because their pack must be a gang. Get some gang bangers to firebomb their hideout.<br /> <br /> Dominate and Majesty are the two best tools in the vampire toolbox, followed closely by Obfuscate and Auspex. Then comes the blood bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T14:10:43-07:00","id":607084,"title":"","content":"This is what the developer said about the comparison between werewolves and vampires and how they handle being 'apex predators.'<br /> <br /> 'An MI6 agent observes a CIA man in 1974 Moscow. She knows what he is \u2014 she can tell by the newspapers he reads, by the routes he drives and what brands of cigarettes he buys on what days. She doesn't need to ask him, and he doesn't need to ask her.<br /> <br /> Every month or so, they meet in a park; mostly, they exchange pleasantries and empty platitudes. Sometimes they share information \u2014 or disinformation \u2014 but broadly, they both have the same goal. She may set a bomb under a junior minister's car; he may spend a night with a senior security guard, turning him into a double agent. Their methods are different, but they both want the same thing in the end. They come from different places, but you can recognize them by their similarities as much as their differences.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:08:16-07:00","id":608628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=606877#post606877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the whole Werewolves are better combatants than Vampires in Gauru forum. The key phrase here is &quot;in Gauru form&quot;, in all other forms Werewolves are squishy, and vulnerable to normal amounts of damage (as opposed to Gauru, which is vulnerable only to absurd amounts of damage). So it behooves a Vampire to avoid direct combat in favor of ambush tactics and coercion.<br /> <br /> However, if a vampire does have to fight a Werewolf head to head, the following approaches work best:<ul><li><b>Bring Friends</b>: Gauru form is absurdly durable, a single vampire is not likely to be able to put the damage forward to pierce its regeneration. Not unless they are some twinked out combat beast. So numbers are your friend. Three people with fully automatic rifles turns the tables quite nicely, though the more the merrier in this endeavor.</li> <li><b>Bring Banes: </b>Silver hurts Werewolves, sometimes it can be enough to deter a fight outright. Remember, every aggravated damage dealt to a wolf decreases the difficulty of rolling over with lethal, so just two or three swipes with a silver knife could be enough to turn the tide (though close quarters combat is highly inadvisable).</li> <li><b>Be a Cheat: </b>Vampires are well equipped to shut down conflicts through mental tricks, Majesty can remove the enemy's incentive to fight, while Obfuscate can remove their ability to attack you (being an invisible sneak). Two dots of Nightmare shuts down just about any combatant, sending the big bad wolf running with its tail between its legs.</li> <li><b>Be a Bad Enough Dude: </b>A suitably combat spec'd Vampire can do toe to toe with a Werewolf, even a very potent one. But this sort of character will probably be rare among PCs, requiring many dots worth of disciplines and devotions to pull off.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Control the terms of the fight. Bring it into a public place, where the risk of Kuruth is just too high to use the Gauru form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T17:26:44-07:00","id":608644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s#post606808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi all, I have a question about aggravated damage. How can a kindred make aggravated damage without using fire or silver but just with his own discipline?<br /> In the first edition the claw made with protean could...but in blod&amp;smoke the claw of protean 2 deal just lethal (banshing against kindred) damage and with protean 4 lethal also against kindred.<br /> In a fight against a werewolf in warform is impossible to win cause he automatically heal ALL lethal damage. I read in the core that some kindred power deal aggravated to the werewolf but I didn' t find that power. And how can werewolf deal aggravated to the kindred ? (With what gift?)<br /> Thank you</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that in second edition, fire does <i>not </i>generally cause aggravated damage to werewolves. <br /> <br /> As stated in Werewolf 2e, p.94,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Aggravated Damage: Aggravated damage regenerates much<br /> slower, closer to the speed of human wounds. Uratha heal one<br /> point of aggravated damage every four days. <b>Only silver and<br /> supernatural powers (including Gifts, mage spells, and vampiric<br /> Disciplines) can cause aggravated damage to Uratha directly.<br /> Any source of harm that would cause aggravated damage to a<br /> human, including massive bodily devastation, only causes lethal<br /> damage to Uratha.</b> As such, most unwitting attackers must do<br /> enough lethal damage to cause it to \u201croll over\u201d into aggravated<br /> damage before it poses a real problem for werewolves. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:05:04-07:00","id":608727,"title":"","content":"Mortals don't even take aggravated from fire, 'just' lethal. Vampires, mummies and prometheans are the only player splats that do.<br /> <br /> Also just to throw this out there, some werewolves are triggered by the presence of other supernaturals. Triggered into Kuruth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T18:43:59-07:00","id":608757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=608628#post608628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Control the terms of the fight. Bring it into a public place, where the risk of Kuruth is just too high to use the Gauru form.</div> </div> </div> </div>And lets not forget the most important, and oft overlooked: have a storyteller and players who want to have interesting, narratively impactful fights.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T20:15:08-07:00","id":615942,"title":"","content":"My players' vampires took down a raging werewolf. Wasn't easy, but there were two vampires, and they brought along a pair of National Guardsmen that one of the vampires had Dominated for that purpose. They did it by filling it so full of lead each round that wraparound damage took its toll. Once stuff starts turning Aggravated, the werewolf's death spiral has begun and it's progressively easier to meet that minimum threshold each round. The trick is to survive that long.<br /> <br /> In the end the Guardsmen even survived, though one was horribly mauled\u2014as was one of the vampires, but that was only a momentary setback for him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-06T17:15:32-07:00","id":618237,"title":"","content":"A sole raging werewolf against four competent combatants isn't likely to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:23:38-07:00","id":619548,"title":"","content":"My question is what does it take (rules wise) to cut of a limb with a weapon like... say a sword?<br /> <br /> And exactly what type of damage is that going to be on a vampire or a werewolf for that matter?<br /> <br /> In real terms it is not actually that hard to cut of a limb with a sharp sword if you hit it from a good angle with enough speed and force. Add powers such as Vigor and it becomes ridiculously easy to do by just hitting something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T16:55:28-07:00","id":619559,"title":"","content":"Cutting of a limb (or permanently damaging it beyond use) is achieved by inflicting more damage than the target's Stamina on a targeted attack that inflicts aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> I would say this works in the same way for vampires and werewolves, with the caveat that mundane sources of aggravated damage inflict only lethal on vampires and werewolves and would not severe limbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T17:06:28-07:00","id":619566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JorgenCAB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=619548#post619548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question is what does it take (rules wise) to cut of a limb with a weapon like... say a sword?<br /> <br /> And exactly what type of damage is that going to be on a vampire or a werewolf for that matter?<br /> <br /> In real terms it is not actually that hard to cut of a limb with a sharp sword if you hit it from a good angle with enough speed and force. Add powers such as Vigor and it becomes ridiculously easy to do by just hitting something.</div> </div> </div> </div>For humans it takes aggravated damage greater than the target's stamina at a -2 called shot penalty to cut off an arm or a leg, 1 aggravated at a -3 called shot penalty to cut off a hand. Weapons just make it easier because they increase your damage dealt on a hit and always deal lethal. There's no rule for decapitation, but you could probably rule that it would be possible with agg greater than the target's stamina at a -3 called shot penalty if you wanted. Personally, I'd only allow it on a Killing Blow, not in normal combat. Since vampires downgrade mundane sources of aggravated damage to lethal and lethal to bashing, I would only require lethal to do it to a vampire so that it isn't harder to cut a vampire's arms off than a human's (barring Resilience).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 08-07-2015, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T01:18:39-07:00","id":619870,"title":"","content":"Well... I think there should be a different case between a sharp bladed weapon doing aggravated damage to a limb in this scenario versus guns or blunt weapons that do damage in a much different way.<br /> <br /> Sure... a vampire might not take as much damage from cuts in muscle tissue and things like that, but a cut off arm is a cut off arm. It would also be so much easier to cut off a limb using a sharp bladed cutting weapon than a blunt weapon like a baseball bat and should be much more dangerous weapon to a vampire since they have such potential to do devastating damage. A fit vampire with some Vigor and blood pumped into strength should basically cut bodies in half with a sword with almost no effort (unless supernatural defenses of course).<br /> <br /> I do think it shouldn't be unreasonable to deem an attack with a bladed cutting weapon that is a called shot to be deemed aggravated damage if a certain number of successes was rolled and enough damage done.. but that would be a house rule I guess for specific cases. But the aggravated damage would only amount to the necessary to cut off the limb... any other damage would still be lethal in that case.<br /> <br /> Large cutting weapons should also be much more dangerous to vampires than weapons such as knives, clubs or other no cutting weapons with the means to do real devastating physical harm. I would not be a stranger to allow cutting weapons to do chunks of Lethal damage to vampires if sustained in enough quantities from any attack. At least part of it should become lethal, say anything above stamina is deemed lethal on a vampire. But that would also be a house rule of mine. Cutting swords are really devastating weapons to unprotected flesh and bone targets... blunt weapons that mainly maim and do internal bleeding wounds are not as dangerous to things such as a vampire as that of a sword.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T04:49:45-07:00","id":619920,"title":"","content":"1- The system seems to care more about usefulness of a limb than it actually being there. An arm crippled by a blunt weapon that just dealt agg damage is pretty much as useless as if it had fallen off. Depending on caliber, a gunshot CAN blow your arm off;<br /> <br /> 2- Such effect would be better delivered by a tilt built in the weapon description, making it mechanically an individual property of the weapon. Given 1, it is more probable that it is a tilt with related Persistent Condition (since arms don't grow up, usually);<br /> <br /> 3- Given balance, mechanical issues, and the overall state of the system, it is probably not worth an actual rule, unless you want to see it play out in your games. You don't need actual house-rules for this kind of effect if you want them to play out just rarely as GM Fiat effects for dramatic scenes. That can be easily done with player agreement and without rules. You need to house-rule it only if you want a common combat to have such risk in your game. And to see your players actually calling shots to cut-off arms.<br /> <br /> 4- During normal combat you can give through description the reasons for the called shot not really cutting an arm off. Just remember that the system doesn't care so much for precision, so you can describe a lot of outcomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T05:28:01-07:00","id":619933,"title":"","content":"You are probably right... it might be more for dramatic effect rather than a general rule. I just like to use bladed weapons being as lethal as they should be. A bladed weapon should be more dangerous than regular gunshots and blunt trauma wounds in general on vampires and even werewolves. On humans I don't think it matter all that much rules wise.<br /> <br /> Sure... a gunshot wound could result in an arm being forced to amputation but to rip an arm off you need a really big weapon. To shop an arm clean of with an axe or blunt weapon is very hard to achieve in a moving fight if not next to impossible, but the effect of a tilt are perhaps the same. It is the cutting force of a sharp blade that is needed to cut bone and flesh clean off though.<br /> <br /> I would not be a stranger to allowing a strong vampire to simply slice a person in half with a sword, not so hard to do given the strength they possess. You might argue it is a Death Blow or something similar, but with a sword this is doable even in combat given the right opportunity and enough force.<br /> <br /> I might simply devise a system of sharp bladed cutting weapons getting some Tilt/Condition with enough successes and damage in a single round. I would say three successes and damage at least higher than the opponent Stamina means a limb is cut of... more than double Stamina in one turn and it simply is a killing blow. But it has to be on a called shot with a -2 penalty. Otherwise the sword work as normal. This way it would not happen very often but still make it possible if attempted by a good swordsman.<br /> <br /> Most of the time you don't even want to cut of someones limbs... so it really needs to be intentional for the most part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T06:52:14-07:00","id":619969,"title":"","content":"At some point, realism needs to give way to the fact that it's a game, and a game where player characters can easily have their limbs cut off in normal combat is just not that much fun for the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:59:17-07:00","id":620209,"title":"","content":"Each chronicle is a world in itself, so I'm not against devising it as a tilt for use in your own games. It isn't worth an official rule, but not hard to achieve with little tinkering and a tilt + Condition.<br /> <br /> I would only advise caution, or the cutting off of pieces of people can become a problem in the game. More than once RPGs tried rules for decapitation, just to drop them later because they rendered the entire combat system moot. I would limit it to limbs, at least, under the assumption that an actual decapitation is so hard to achieve it would only occur rules-wise when the damage kills the subject anyway (so it is just a way to describe the final blow). The same for any cut that should result in insta-death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T11:00:43-07:00","id":620296,"title":"","content":"Well... it is up the the storyteller to not use such rules in any excessive way. The same goes for player characters... they will certainly get in trouble if they go around chopping peoples arms off left and right just because they can... and if they can they probably could kill as easily and they will not do that too often either.<br /> <br /> I personally try to retain as much realism as I can in order to make things dark, gritty and dangerous. Makes players think before they act... being a vampire also makes physical aggression quite forgiving anyway.... if you play a mortal then you really need to be cautious... that's just the way it is.<br /> <br /> I'm perfectly fine with having it as a house rule though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T11:49:42-07:00","id":620348,"title":"","content":"On the one hand, dismembering a character that can regrow limbs is generally not going to ruin their player's experience. On the other, do it too often and it will begin to seem like a running gag, which can jar with the mood somewhat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T14:51:35-07:00","id":620566,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with Elfive. Sometimes dismember a PC or a PNC help to give the right horror atmosphere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T14:52:52-07:00","id":620568,"title":"","content":"Is this not true for all types of combat or power usage?<br /> <br /> It is up to the ST to maintain a balance of power abuse to make things mysterious and intriguing. You don't accomplish that by repeating the same thing over and over and I don*t hold this particular stunt more special than anything else you can throw at the players.<br /> <br /> How often are NPCs going to be armed with swords AND able to perform this maneuver?<br /> <br /> We don't usually run high powered campaigns and NPCs with skills to routinely shop off another vampires arm would be in very short supply. We do have one player character that is an expert swordsman though... a Mekhet assassin. Probably one of the few kindred in the city skilled enough to perform such maneuvers in a combat situation. This is one of the reasons we looked at the rules and usefulness of swords in general for vampires. We have not used any special rules yet... it's not like he get to use his weapon all that much anyway. He is one of those... if he draws his blade he intend to kill with it so he fight with the sword still in the sheath (which need to be replaced from time to time). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:06:04-07:00","id":620599,"title":"","content":"The advice sums to just one principle:<br /> <br /> If this thing becomes visibly more powerful than regular combat, expect your players to rely on it over and over.<br /> <br /> Of course, every troupe is different, as is every chronicle. You'll probably be able to handle things, this is just a cautionary advice about how to do the tilt, I do think you should do it if it is good for your troupe's gaming experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T15:38:00-07:00","id":620648,"title":"","content":"Which I agree with to some degree. There need to be a balance so there never are just one way to solve a problem. Swords are kind of hard to run around with, even if you employ Obfuscate to hide them. In Kindred politics you will be spotted and discredited soon enough. So... there are many drawbacks and firearms are still often more useful anyway.<br /> <br /> I don't think player characters would run around with swords all the time because of rules like this, swords are really impractical tools. Most of the Vampires in our group never carry weapons at all unless they expect to use them for any reason. Even less spending time training with them to improve their skill (use XP to further themselves in the arts of combat).<br /> <br /> Also,,, in the way you gain experience now does not reward meta gaming that much anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T21:43:18-07:00","id":620906,"title":"","content":"Actually, swords are very easy to run around with if you hide them with Obfuscate. As long as you don't attack anyone with it, no one will even notice it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T22:23:17-07:00","id":620920,"title":"","content":"And with Majesty no one will even care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T01:11:12-07:00","id":620993,"title":"","content":"You will get caught with your hand in the cookie jar eventually and that is when the shit hit the fan for bringing deadly weapons to &quot;friendly&quot; gatherings and others domains and becomes a political pariah and known troublemaker. At least that is how it is in our games if you run around armed in other Kindreds domains &quot;openly&quot; and is caught with them. With some exceptions weapons are not allowed in places where kindred tend to mingle. Also, Obfuscate don't work too well on metal detectors either and some Kindred are pretty paranoid and take security pretty seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T05:06:14-07:00","id":621089,"title":"","content":"Ceramic swords. Obfuscate should allow a person to bypass some metal detectors and with higher levels most of them. The TSA couldn't find a weapon on someone most of the time even though people don't have Obfuscate. I'm pretty sure someone aware of Obfuscate powers could come up with a protocol to allow for a roll to find a weapon though.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate tends to work because the chief weapon is surprise...<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7WJXHY2OXGE\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7WJXHY2OXGE\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7WJXHY2OXGE\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7WJXHY2OXGE </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 08-09-2015, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:14:18-07:00","id":621279,"title":"","content":"Actualy Obfuscate wouldn't work even on crappy detectors, because it doesn't work on technology at all.<br /> <br /> BUT it would work on the people using said technology. If the detector causes insta-close of a door, it will work. But if it just sounds an alarm, I'm not sure. The X-Ray system of an airport WOULD be fouled, since it is based on personal observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T08:32:14-07:00","id":621335,"title":"","content":"The way to beat metal detectors while using obfuscate is to make sure you go through with someone else. The detector goes off, they get stopped and you carry on without anyone having noticed you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:04:15-07:00","id":621368,"title":"","content":"You'd probably want to avoid commercial flights like the plague. You don't want to be stuck on the runway when the sun rises due to some poor planning on the airport's behalf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T09:26:39-07:00","id":621404,"title":"","content":"I don't think that anyone in vampire circles are going to blink an eye at someone carrying weapons. Are we going to cut off the hands of anyone that has access to Protean? Remember, vampires only take bashing from bladed weapons - and we all know that several mental disciplines make physical attacks worthless. <br /> <br /> After all, the scariest weapons to a vampire include a moltov, followed by a wooden stake. Last time I checked, we didn't have a wood or alcohol detector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-09-2015, 12:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:02:16-07:00","id":621433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=621335#post621335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way to beat metal detectors while using obfuscate is to make sure you go through with someone else. The detector goes off, they get stopped and you carry on without anyone having noticed you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kindred security is not fooled by that with modern technology and enough paranoia they will care.<br /> <br /> Several kindred in the city we run have advanced surveillance around with computers running face recognition programs etc... when the computer take the decisions Obfuscate is actually hard to use. Every kindred also have to electronically register themselves while entering as well in these places. All for the extra security and keeping the traditions. Some even employ Mekhet doormen to read their mood and categorically turn away kindred with a malicious mood.<br /> <br /> Kindred also have many resources to protect beside their own life and even if Protean and other Kindred powers are impossible to stop it does not mean they will want to reduce the chances of anyone doing damage while maximize their own power to employ it as a host if hostility do arise.<br /> <br /> Even if vampires are to some degree \u201cimmune\u201d to most damage weapons are far from not dangerous in the right hands. It is just plain curtsy that weapons are not carried in other Kindreds domain unless you intend to use them. It is simply a way to show blatant hostility. If that is what you want to achieve then all is fine.<br /> <br /> Given how rare it is for vampires to actually \u201cfight\u201d physically with each other its not strange that weapons are banned in social gatherings as part of cultural traditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7068,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","user":"JorgenCAB","date":". 08-09-2015, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:14:53-07:00","id":621440,"title":"","content":"Right, so a guy with a hand held metal detector will ignore it going off due to Obfuscate. Loud alarms going off when you walk through a gateway is beyond the power, people will notice the alarms. Somebody looking at an x-ray machine won't see an object made invisible, but someone monitoring from another room would. Contrary to normal security that really should rely on trained personnel interacting with people and machines as a backup, Kindred should use remote monitoring and paranoid procedures, as in strip down and put your clothes in the drawer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T10:25:01-07:00","id":621444,"title":"","content":"Yeah... and do you really risk all this just to smuggle in a dagger, sword or pistol which will just lead to you becoming a social Pariah later on or even barred permanently until you redeem yourself. Is it really worth it to prove to your ego you can get away with it if you don't intend to use it.<br /> <br /> Sure... if you have the intent to use the weapon you might have a plan to get a weapon inside... but you are probably better of having someone else smuggle it in using different powers in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7068,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","user":"JorgenCAB","date":". 08-09-2015, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T14:36:12-07:00","id":621630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=621368#post621368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'd probably want to avoid commercial flights like the plague. You don't want to be stuck on the runway when the sun rises due to some poor planning on the airport's behalf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, just plan it well. With Obfuscate or high-level Majesty you can actually arrive at the airport and take whatever flight you want right before it takes off. With some work you'll have a safe heaven for the day at the airport and some safety on some areas of the airplane itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right, so a guy with a hand held metal detector will ignore it going off due to Obfuscate. Loud alarms going off when you walk through a gateway is beyond the power, people will notice the alarms. Somebody looking at an x-ray machine won't see an object made invisible, but someone monitoring from another room would. Contrary to normal security that really should rely on trained personnel interacting with people and machines as a backup, Kindred should use remote monitoring and paranoid procedures, as in strip down and put your clothes in the drawer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, current rules on Obfuscate do let the guys on another room be fooled. But sure, Kindred are aware of such possibilities and can simply employ automated security. If the computer takes the decision, as <b>JorgenCAB</b> said, it won't be fooled.<br /> <br /> I was actually talking about it in a more general sense. Surely, if your city's Kindred are paranoid about weapons, they have plenty of ways to safeguard their heavens and Elysium.<br /> <br /> But, again, I don't think they would do it for a simple cost-benefit relation. Those weapons aren't so dangerous to them. And also, you have tradition. Some vampires are ancient beings, and until little more than a century ago it wasn't so strange to carry weapons regularly with you, specially bladed weapons, from swords to simple knifes. The social rule wasn't about not bringing your weapon, but leaving it at the entrance when arriving. And a break of this rule would have more social consequences than the danger the weapon itself presents.<br /> <br /> So, tough it isn't at all impossible to safeguard against blades, it is <u>usually</u> too much effort than it is worth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T20:18:46-07:00","id":621847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=621630#post621630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, current rules on Obfuscate do let the guys on another room be fooled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where did you come up with that?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T01:39:13-07:00","id":621953,"title":"","content":"The rules do not directly mention how this work but the explanation is that it is the Beast that hide the vampire and the one affected by the vampires Obfuscate must be able to sense the beast somehow. So normal Obfuscate would typically only work on someone in the same room that can hear, smell or feel the vampire in some way. Someone looking at the vampire through a monitor sitting in the same room would be effected like anyone else. I even would say they would ignore subtle alarms such as a beeping sound from a metal detector or just not reflect on the vampire and disregard the event as some malfunction of the equipment.<br /> <br /> I see no reason why a modern vampire could not learn some Vigor+Obfuscate devotion to make anyone watching a monitor in real time also subject to their Obfuscate... but this would probably be a rare and very unknown vampire power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T04:43:34-07:00","id":622058,"title":"","content":"Nevermind it, I just got confused with a piece of text from other book that I thought to remember from B&amp;S. Probably V20 and some confusing with memory. The rules actually aren't clear about the reach of Obfuscate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:19:35-07:00","id":622227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JorgenCAB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=621444#post621444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah... and do you really risk all this just to smuggle in a dagger, sword or pistol which will just lead to you becoming a social Pariah later on or even barred permanently until you redeem yourself. Is it really worth it to prove to your ego you can get away with it if you don't intend to use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would vampires turn someone into a social pariah over a gun or knife? Most vampires laugh it off when attacked - they're more annoyed at the ruined clothes than at the physical damage.<br /> <br /> For Kindred security, its just silly. I can walk in with a wooden stake and your metal detector is worthless. I could make obsidian knives, and the metal detector won't work. I could learn Protean. I could know Blood Scourge or an attack power of Cruac?<br /> <br /> Why should those who focus on physical abilities be handicapped? There's a million ways to get around such a ban, and you're just handicapping those who'd be able to respond to the threat.<br /> <br /> What about situations that call for dueling? The Invictus loves their duels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T07:57:42-07:00","id":622256,"title":"","content":"If the Invictus doesn't consider a sabre worn at the hip acceptable formal wear you're doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T11:53:30-07:00","id":622490,"title":"","content":"The issue with Vampires vs Garou isn't the massive regeneration, it's Hit and Run. Hit and Run allows the Werewolf to perfectly avoid one attack per turn at the low cost of 1e with no limit. It even works against surprise attacks. The only way I know of to stop it is grappling, and even that isn't clear-cut. For punching through regeneration you'll want to use Brawl (bite + feed), Grapple Style 3, Ride the Wave 1, and Professional Training 5 can do it. Melee with a high damage code can do it. Chokehold works against any werewolves with a Stamina of 5 or less in Garou. Vigor is very helpful at all levels. What none of that can do is bypass Hit and Run.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-10-2015, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:24:24-07:00","id":622532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hit and Run allows the Werewolf to perfectly avoid one attack per turn at the low cost of 1e with no limit. <b>It even works against surprise attacks</b><i>.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div>Really? Wow! I\u00b4m no big Garou fan so I don\u00b4t know much but how the hell does that work?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So normal Obfuscate would typically only work on someone in the same room that can hear, smell or feel the vampire in some way. Someone looking at the vampire through a monitor sitting in the same room would be effected like anyone else. </div> </div> </div>I would actually like some kind of clarification about this whole range of obfuscate thing. Might be a worthy question for the FAQ. On the one hand obfuscate is very strong right now. On the other I am not sure if I like easy technical bypasses. The whole damn survailance thing is already a big headach for a game about monsters living secretly among us as it is. Making it even more powerful seems especially bad for more &quot;classic&quot; nosferatu character-concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2158-saimid","name":"Saimid","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T12:31:26-07:00","id":622547,"title":"","content":"Personally I've already house ruled that Hit and Run requires a successful attack. So, you know, you have to <b>Hit</b> and Run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T13:18:36-07:00","id":622600,"title":"","content":"Does Hit and Run bypass a bullet?<br /> <br /> I'm not even talking about a silvered one.<br /> <br /> What about an entire coterie worth of bullets?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:08:39-07:00","id":622706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=622227#post622227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would vampires turn someone into a social pariah over a gun or knife? Most vampires laugh it off when attacked - they're more annoyed at the ruined clothes than at the physical damage.<br /> <br /> For Kindred security, its just silly. I can walk in with a wooden stake and your metal detector is worthless. I could make obsidian knives, and the metal detector won't work. I could learn Protean. I could know Blood Scourge or an attack power of Cruac?<br /> <br /> Why should those who focus on physical abilities be handicapped? There's a million ways to get around such a ban, and you're just handicapping those who'd be able to respond to the threat.<br /> <br /> What about situations that call for dueling? The Invictus loves their duels.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's about tradition and carrying weapons (even a wooden stake) is seen as bad form. It also is an enabler of violence. It has nothing to do with vampiric powers which is something no one can control.<br /> <br /> Vampires simply don't generally allow weapons by guests or in Elysium type areas.<br /> <br /> It is also a way to reduce harm against mortal servants and allies... or at least reduce the risks.<br /> <br /> There is nothing magic about this at all.and where do you draw the line?<br /> Can they walk into Elysium and others domains with bombs, grenades and machine-guns to... I mean they all do bashing... just shit loads of it. Where do you draw the line... most vampires just say NO weapons to make it clear.<br /> <br /> This way the host will be able to keep the edge if a violent confrontation do occur.<br /> <br /> Then there is also the traditions which are quite harsh against killed vampires. Violence between kindred can easily spiral out of control and that is bad for everyone. Vampires are immortal and physical violence are rarely something they resort to and is why it usually are looked down upon in general as crude. Duels are most likely very rare and when they do happen it is the event of the decade.<br /> <br /> I understand that every vampire chronicle is different but from most of the material that I have read Vampires rarely destroy or attack each other personally and it is mostly younger vampires that use violence to gain something. Every violent situation do mean an unnecessary risk, most older vampires managed to get there by removing themselves from such risks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T15:27:56-07:00","id":622720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=622600#post622600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Hit and Run bypass a bullet?<br /> <br /> I'm not even talking about a silvered one.<br /> <br /> What about an entire coterie worth of bullets?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. If you want you could use Fog of War and make that coterie worth of bullets hit one member.<br /> <br /> @Saimid: It's an interrupt. When an attack is occurring they jump ahead in the queue, act before the attack. Celerity does the same thing, Hit and Run just comes with a bonus if you pull it off.<br /> <br /> @Many: It's Werewolf or Uratha for the entire race, Gauru for the name of the war form. Garou are in Werewolf the Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T16:54:16-07:00","id":622829,"title":"","content":"Well, given claims that Obfuscate is potentially overpowered, I re-read the disciplines. A few points I noticed:<br /> <br /> The first dot can be broken if you do anything to gain attention or are somewhere nobody expects to find anyone. I'd personally count setting off a metal detector as doing something to gain attention. Being there when nobody sent anyone through the metal detector could also count as being somewhere nobody expects someone to be. Of course, both probably up to Storyteller.<br /> <br /> Second can be broken by being forced to interact. I guess getting frisked would probably break it (only works on items).<br /> <br /> Third still has incidental signs. I'd say metal detector counts.So you'd still hear it even if you couldn't break the obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Familiar Stranger is probably your best bet. Disguise the item as something innocuous. Seems like it can't be broken by any means whatsoever. That said, it's the fourth dot. Most people aren't going to get that anytime soon.<br /> <br /> Fifth dot is entirely irrelevant to this discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T17:12:22-07:00","id":622845,"title":"","content":"Yeah, just going through by yourself wouldn't work. Hence the sleight of hand. (Sleight of foot?) The idea is that the obfuscate holds because the attention can be redirected to <i>someone else.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T01:14:35-07:00","id":623191,"title":"","content":"If you are a guest in someone else domain you just should respect their wishes or not show up at all. Are you there to cause trouble or not?<br /> <br /> If you cheat your way in and is later caught what have you really accomplished?<br /> <br /> If you are suppose to register at the front door and don't and the host approach you and ask why you did not submit your invitation at the door, have you actually gained anything but suspicion and resentment. Perhaps they frisk you just to make sure you didn't smuggle in something dangerous and asks his security to review the tapes and look at what you have done while being there.<br /> <br /> All this just to smuggle in a weapon you most probably will never use anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T04:07:41-07:00","id":623208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JorgenCAB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=622706#post622706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about tradition and carrying weapons (even a wooden stake) is seen as bad form. It also is an enabler of violence. It has nothing to do with vampiric powers which is something no one can control.</div> </div> </div> </div> Vampire tradition actually supports carrying weapons, in the case of Invictus Knights. <i>Grabbing</i> the weapon while staring at someone is a different matter. Anyone who's being disarmed will simply find a way around the &quot;bad form.&quot; It is foolish to rely on the good will of other vampires. You can forbid discipline use or weapon carry all you want. That just means people will be subtle about it. These are vampires we're talking about. They don't play nice, and they only follow the so-called rules on the surface.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There is nothing magic about this at all.and where do you draw the line? Can they walk into Elysium and others domains with bombs, grenades and machine-guns to... I mean they all do bashing... just shit loads of it. Where do you draw the line... most vampires just say NO weapons to make it clear. </div> </div> </div> <i>They're vampires.</i> By nature, everything is about magic.<br /> <br /> As for the line? The line in Elysium has always been the same thing - no physical violence. Threats have always been a staple of Elysium, however. Just because the knight's sword is bound while inside Elysium doesn't mean he won't follow you once you leave it. Its a statement.<br /> <br /> Your grenades and machine gun issue is more of a question of attracting unwanted attention, not inciting violence. And, sure, the harpies will mock you for doing it, but that's their job.<br /> <br /> And, for the record, guns are overrated. A vampire with a bit of Vigor can deal more damage to a fellow vampire with a blade than even the most powerful rifle can. We currently have no rules for grenades, so we have no idea how strong they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then there is also the traditions which are quite harsh against killed vampires. </div> </div> </div> There is no such thing. There are three Traditions in Requiem - Masquerade, Progeny, and Diablarie. The haven's &quot;castle doctrine&quot; - the idea that a vampire's haven is his personal domain and can set any rule he can enforce inside it - is a close fourth. There is no Destruction tradition in Requiem. While the Lance tends to preach against killing other vampires, there's nothing to suggest that other domains feel the same.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Violence between kindred can easily spiral out of control and that is bad for everyone. Vampires are immortal and physical violence are rarely something they resort to and is why it usually are looked down upon in general as crude. Duels are most likely very rare and when they do happen it is the event of the decade. </div> </div> </div> Ummmm..... Physical violence is something they rarely resort to? Are we playing the same game here? Violence is epidemic in vampire culture. That's why frenzy is a thing - because you push a vampire far enough that they lash out and attack. Every interaction with another vampire carries the threat of physical violence under it. That's why Elysium needs to ban physical violence - because its about the only place <i>safe</i> to interact without violence happening. And, even then, its a fragile safety, only as strong as the enforcement of the Keeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you cheat your way in and is later caught what have you really accomplished? </div> </div> </div> Then don't get caught. Its that simple, really. And what have you accomplished? Having a back up way of defending yourself to and from Elysium, or if something goes to hell in a handbasket. <br /> <br /> Remember, you can get away with just about anything in vampire society if you can blame someone else loud enough to drown out the talk about you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T04:38:44-07:00","id":623216,"title":"","content":"I simply don't think we play with the same setting... in our world vampires do care and do enforce no weapon rules in their own domain and Elysiums by other vampires not in their leash. As a safety measure to have the edge. If you don't follow the rules you simply are not welcome. If you are an Invictus Knight you just leave your weapons at the door or wherever... when you leave you may do whatever you wish, or you simply don't attend these gatherings. Your choice...<br /> <br /> Violence is not common at all between vampires in our chronicles for the simple reason they want to survive. They send allies, retainers and other thugs to do their dirty works. Only a stupid vampire will risk their immortal life unless it is absolutely necessary. If there is violence it is usually the young vampires doing something as a favor to an older vampire. The younger vampires have usually not matured enough to grasp the importance of survival... they are like human teenagers.<br /> <br /> The right of destruction are mostly between sire and child and for the most part the Prince will not tolerate wanton destruction of kindred outside this parameter unless it is sanctioned by him. But sure... it happens anyway.<br /> <br /> And.. I really don't care if Vigor or Protean are potentially more dangerous than a gun... a gun is still an enabler of violence you can remove from the picture. Guns are also more lethal to human allies and retainers which you might also want to protect in these areas as much as possible.<br /> It is also easier to restrain a marauding vampire if they are not wielding a sword than if they do, especially for a group of Ghouls.<br /> <br /> There are many reasons why they would enforce a no weapon rule. If there is a no violence rule there are no reason to not have a no weapon rule as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7068-jorgencab","name":"JorgenCAB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T07:53:17-07:00","id":623298,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're playing the same game, you two are just coming at it from different angles. This shouldn't be a surprise and certainly shouldn't be leading to accusations of one person doing it wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T10:09:07-07:00","id":623419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=622490#post622490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The issue with Vampires vs Garou isn't the massive regeneration, it's Hit and Run. Hit and Run allows the Werewolf to perfectly avoid one attack per turn at the low cost of 1e with no limit. It even works against surprise attacks. The only way I know of to stop it is grappling, and even that isn't clear-cut.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hit &amp; Run is one Facet of one Gift - not every werewolf is going to have it.<br /> <br /> And, really, it isn't that much more powerful than Celerity - it has some additional benefits Celerity doesn't, and can be used an unlimited number of times, but it is also less flexible. I'm not sure where the idea it for sure works against surprise attacks comes in - I think that would be very much Storyteller's call. Just because something is Reflexive doesn't mean it can be used in all situations.<br /> <br /> It also may not defend well against ranged attacks, depending on the landscape. And if the opponent is going before the werewolf, it may also foil the werewolf's attack - unless the werewolf gets an exceptional success, I'd definitely say the movement from Hit &amp; Run is his movement for the turn, so the werewolf is probably going to end up not being in a position to attack, depending on who goes when. It is a really nice Gift, but it certainly isn't a bigger advantage than, say, Garou form.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T11:18:04-07:00","id":623500,"title":"","content":"There are plenty reasons for vampires to forbid weapons at their Domains. There are plenty reasons for the to do not. Probably there are plenty of Domains under each assumption.<br /> <br /> But my point is just that it is too much effort and cost to place so much defenses against weapons in every Elysium. Even the richest ones rarely will go so far. A vampire with high Auspex is far more reliable than all those, and far cheaper once you know the guy.<br /> <br /> Vampires are able to survive a weapon without much effort. They're also able to perceive and socially punish lack of decorum easier. There are no sense to go so far to prevent it from happening to begin with, because it is too much effort, cost and attention for almost no effect.<br /> <br /> Yes, frequently bringing weapons WILL be considered bad form. At least you'll be expected to leave the weapon at the entrance. But vampires don't need to actually go so far to prevent it from happening. Someone who do that will eventually be discovered, and them at least mocked, if not expelled and exiled from Elysium, or even severely punished. Given that, doing so would be such a problem that the Keeper actually don't need to harass so much the attendees for them to not bring weapons. They won't, because it isn't worth it. And those security measures would be a lot more uncomfortable to them than the possibility of maybe someone being stupid to bring weapons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T12:16:31-07:00","id":623580,"title":"","content":"There's plenty of reasons to go to extreme lengths to bar or allow weapons at Elysium. The VII can be a faction of brainwashed vampires who might be activated at any moment to kill other vampires. A good moment might be when everyone else is disarmed and thinking they're going to 'laugh off' being hurt. Cainites can keep vampires from moving past a line and enhance weapons to do lethal damage. Mythologies offers an entire faction of rogue ghouls for you to use. Four of the five primary covenants are constantly at odds with another covenant directly opposed to their ideals. Werewolves could be just around the corner, as can mages, strix, hunters, Beasts and any number of other supernaturals who have potentially infinite reasons for wanting to destroy vampires.<br /> <br /> There's no reason to jump on someone just because they're not playing the game the same way as you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-11-2015, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T12:29:30-07:00","id":623586,"title":"","content":"Those sound like reasons to allow weapons at Elysium to me, nofather.<br /> <br /> I think there will be Elysiums that allow all weapons, certain weapons, or none at all. I think it will have more to do with the whims of the powers at be than anything else. Since vampires have natural weapons (fangs), I'm pretty sure the penalty for violence in Elysium would be the reason not to <i>use</i> a weapon even if you bring one. If the penalty for violating Elysium sanctuary isn't sufficient to keep the peace then I don't see how banning weapons is going to help. History shows banning weapons does nothing to curb violence. Laws show people don't read enough about history. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> In character any position is fine, but out of character either the honor code or a strong Prince are going to keep peace in Elysium, not security checkpoints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T12:44:14-07:00","id":623589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=623586#post623586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sound like reasons to allow weapons at Elysium to me, nofather.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't want the court's duelist armed when her eyes get glassy and she turns all Reggie Jackson from Naked Gun.<br /> <br /> Of course all it would take is a Carthian enacting Establish Precedent to bar anyone from using or bringing weapons to Elysium.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T13:21:56-07:00","id":623614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=623589#post623589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't want the court's duelist armed when her eyes get glassy and she turns all Reggie Jackson from Naked Gun.<br /> <br /> Of course all it would take is a Carthian enacting Establish Precedent to bar anyone from using or bringing weapons to Elysium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the flexible nature in the definition of weapons, I think a Precedent that bars physical violence at Elysium would be wiser. A dozen people with shotguns would make short work of the duelist. I assume the penalty for any serious physical assaults at Elysium is final death in most domains. Either way, the duelist could have a ceramic sword or get a Sanctified to transform a sword into something innocuous. Any security can be beaten. Heavy security can't be placed in a public meeting place. Too many problems for too little gain. However, a Prince might just not like guns, so he bans them from Elysium. There are reasons to ban weapons. Preventing violence isn't a good one. History has shown when you effectively ban weapons the people you don't want to have weapons simply learn to use farming tools, whatever is at hand, and unarmed fighting to lethal efficiency. It doesn't stop people from trying to make it work though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T13:38:40-07:00","id":623635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=623614#post623614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the flexible nature in the definition of weapons, I think a Precedent that bars physical violence at Elysium would be wiser. A dozen people with shotguns would make short work of the duelist. I assume the penalty for any serious physical assaults at Elysium is final death in most domains. Either way, the duelist could have a ceramic sword or get a Sanctified to transform a sword into something innocuous. Any security can be beaten. Heavy security can't be placed in a public meeting place. Too many problems for too little gain. However, a Prince might just not like guns, so he bans them from Elysium. There are reasons to ban weapons. Preventing violence isn't a good one. History has shown when you effectively ban weapons the people you don't want to have weapons simply learn to use farming tools, whatever is at hand, and unarmed fighting to lethal efficiency. It doesn't stop people from trying to make it work though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or the dozen people with shotguns could be the VII assassins.<br /> <br /> While preventing physical violence might be a better way to go, I don't believe using a ceramic sword or temporarily hiding the weapon in the form of something else would sneak by it. And it's certainly a ST decision, but bringing farming tools to use as weapons would probably count as well.<br /> <br /> What doesn't help is that a piece of wood or a flame can be the most devastating weapons to vampires, and the former you'd be likely to find at Elysium even if it took some smashing and the latter can be created any number of ways.<br /> <br /> That all said I certainly agree, there'd be Elysium that allow all weapons, some, or none.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T23:47:25-07:00","id":623954,"title":"","content":"Nothing against some Elysium not allowing weapons, at the Keeper's discretion.<br /> <br /> I just think that heavy security measures to prevent weapons is too much a cost to be a <u>common</u> feature. It isn't worth, given all variables.<br /> <br /> But sure, some Domains can even have this level of security as an actual requisite for a meeting be considered Elysium, because the Powers That Be just want this for whatever reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T00:23:22-07:00","id":623983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/606808-aggravated-damage-source-in-b-s?p=623954#post623954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing against some Elysium not allowing weapons, at the Keeper's discretion.<br /> <br /> I just think that heavy security measures to prevent weapons is too much a cost to be a <u>common</u> feature. It isn't worth, given all variables.<br /> <br /> But sure, some Domains can even have this level of security as an actual requisite for a meeting be considered Elysium, because the Powers That Be just want this for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, seems like a lot of expense for pretty minimal benefit, especially since at the end of the day, if someone <i>really</i> wants to get a weapon in there, they'll find a way. I'm sure there are domains where the powers that be are paranoid enough that they will go to any lengths to keep weapons out of Elysium. There are probably even more that have it as a general rule, but have minimal measures to prevent it. And certainly some that just don't even care, bring what ever weapons you want as long as you don't use them. All of the arguments that have been presented here in this thread seem like they'd work just fine as in-character reasoning a Keeper of Elysium might use to justify their security measures or lack thereof. Different domains 'gonna have different rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T18:32:43-07:00","id":627158,"title":"","content":"What about a vamp with briefcase full of wooden #2 pencils?(the Kevin Grey attack)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0